{
  "id": "Compound::DB00425 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Zolpidem, a central nervous system sedative, is linked to Cyp3a4 through a series of enzymatic activities. The evidence suggests that Zolpidem binds to Cyp3a7 and Cyp2c9, which in turn participate in metabolic processes involving oxidoreductase, aromatase, and monooxygenase activities. These activities are ultimately linked to Cyp3a4, indicating a potential role for these enzymes in the metabolism of Zolpidem. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Zolpidem is processed in the body, with Cyp3a4 playing a central role in its metabolic fate. The evidence supports a dependency on Cyp3a4 for the enzymatic transformation of Zolpidem, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
